Wait for a builder to exit after it closes its output (NixOS/nix#2176).

On EOF on the builder's output the build goal killed the builder, so one that
closes its output before its last process exits (coreutils does at exit) failed
with signal 9. The worker now holds that EOF back until the builder has exited,
a pidfd in its poll set, or until builder-exit-timeout (default 10 s; 0 = old
behavior) has passed, so other goals keep running meanwhile. The builder stays
unreaped until then: its own exit status is reported and leftover processes are
still killed. Without pidfd_open (Linux < 5.3, other Unixes) unprepareBuild()
waits instead, bounded by the same setting.

